# rm234, the square of blue (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm234
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rmx_rika_gullwell
written_by codex
title the square of blue
fits stage=adult|old
prefers temper=short drive=ambitious
traits temper=short talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=ambitious
quirk keeps_one_blue_patch_to_test_how_the_light_takes_a_colour
likes plum_tart singing new_boots first_warm_day
dislikes rats drizzle
fears steam_without_a_window stall_rent_rising
hopes a_counter_under_a_blue_awning
topics work +0.5 dreams +0.4 weather +0.3 food +0.2 gossip -0.3
styles comfort=plain gossip=closed refuse=sharp tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# holds a square of blue against the light before judging a colour, sings the breath back after a cough, and measures market fronts in lengths of cloth.

words
oath! = Soap on silk | Fray the blue
saying! = Test a corner before the lot | Blue in a shadow buys nothing
square = my blue test piece | a thumb-square of blue
plum = the sharp skin | a plum skin curled in pastry
ropepeg = a blunt wooden peg | a peg darkened by use
steam = a lick of grey steam | a cloud warm as breath
rinse = the second rinse | water clear down to a pin
coinbag = a knotted scrap | my leather corners
crossstitch = a blue cross | two blue stitches
tuneend = my lowest note | the held end of a verse
hem = a strong hem | the lip of a cotton strip
splinter = a pale splinter | the tip of a wood shaving
shopline = a length of red twine | the cord from my pocket

any
opinion @1 dole for 2 : I've made a free bowl last through a long afternoon. Let folk have a bowl without a lecture.
opinion @1 city for 2 : Ridgemere can give the same bit of cloth six colours in one street. I'd miss that changing light.
opinion @1 houses against 3 : A fine crest needs washing like any plain front. That should tell the Houses something.
opinion @1 merchants against 2 : A loaf costs more each time I reach for my dry purse.
opinion @1 festivals against 2 : All that bunting to bring in wet afterwards. I can think of happier uses for a song.
opinion @1 sump for 1 : There's room for another peg on our lines if folk hang things straight.
opinion @1 newcomers against 1 : I wish the city put fresh jobs out with the welcome.

grown
line @1 greet : Your face shows clear against these bricks.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : Clean space by the wall if you want it.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. The blue's still grey.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening suits a plain dark shade.
line @1 greet.return : Ah, your face has come into the light.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : Come near. I'd recognise your tread in thick fog.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : Mind my elbows. You've got my ears.
line @4 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : By lamplight I recognise voices sooner.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Move close enough to share a family word.
line @1 again.open : Found a minute the steam hasn't swallowed yet.
line @1 hail [pair.band=friends] : There! Keep the blue square in sight.
line @1 farewell : Give your coat a shake going out.
line @1 farewell.return : And let your sleeves dry before you fold them.
line @1 react.news : Which bit reached your ears plainest?
line @1 react.news.new : That hasn't hung on any line I've passed.
line @1 react.news.known : The same account reached my ears before the cloth dried.
line @1 react.news.doubt : Hold it up against another account first.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Grief can wring every bit of strength away.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : The whole street looks a shade brighter for that.
line @1 ask.how : How's your wind holding up today?
line @1 answer.how : Taut as a line, but holding.
line @1 thank : You eased a knot I couldn't reach.
line @1 deflect_thanks : The dry end was handy in my paw.
line @1 sympathise : Sit by a little warmth. I'll see to the noise.
line @1 reassure : There's a breath left for the next bit.
line @1 decline : I'll keep my strength for the work I've taken on.
line @1 accept_decline : Keep your reason. Your word will do.
line @1 preclose : I want the good light for my next errand.
line @1 accept_preclose : I'll take my end of the talk in now too.
scene cheap_dye
when topic=work|smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Put blue beside a cheap black. | I've been carrying #square# so long the fold is white.
b : What happens to the black? | Does that spoil the test?
a : Turns brown before your eyes. You can spend your money elsewhere. | Gives me a second test. I know how white ought to look too.

scene level_with_eye
when topic=work self.working=yes self.job=laborer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've had cloth look clean below my waist and grey at eye level. | Hold the bundle away from your apron.
b : Which height do you trust? | To keep the apron dry?
a : The one where a customer will see it. | To keep the apron from lending its colour to the bundle.

scene stall_front
when topic=dreams
does confide / react.self / assess
a : My counter will stand just high enough to lean on, someday. | One striped awning would suit my stall.
b : You've measured it already. | That sounds costly.
a : With my elbow against half the ledges in town. | I'll buy it plain and stitch those stripes on in the evenings.

scene throat_song
when topic=health|pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The low end of a song fits a scratch in the throat. | I've a verse that starts right down by my boot soles.
b : Why keep singing? | Can you reach the note?
a : If my throat's set on making a noise, let it carry my tune. | On a damp day I practically live there.

scene tart_end
when topic=food self.likes=plum_tart
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My favourite taste is #plum# with a little flour along one edge. | A plum tart travels badly in a pocket.
b : Burnt flour? | How do you carry yours?
a : Just caught. It puts the sweetness in its place. | With a bite missing every ten steps.

scene boots_step
when topic=pastimes self.likes=new_boots
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like a boot with enough voice to answer the cobbles. | New boots change the height of every sill.
b : A squeak? | By that much?
a : A sharp little knock. I paid for those soles. | If you're airing the toes on one, half an inch matters.

scene soft_spring
when topic=season here.season=spring
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : I wait till the little hollows behind my knees feel warm. | Fresh air between an open coat and a dry shirt. That's spring enough.
b : That's an odd place to feel spring. | You wear simple pleasures well.
a : The wind reaches everywhere else first. | I worked for the dry shirt.

scene thin_drizzle
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Rain that never quite falls is my least favourite trick. | A shower gives you a good excuse to stop. This just settles in the stitches.
b : How do you tell it's there? | Surely you can shelter?
a : The back of my paw goes dark. Nothing to shake off. | I'd spend all day starting and stopping.

scene rat_lid
when topic=animals self.dislikes=rats
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A pot lid against the flour bin makes a fine rat alarm. | I take pains with the lowest shelf of any cupboard.
b : A bell won't do? | Why there first?
a : I'm not giving a rat an instrument. | A rat can climb, but it would rather walk in.

scene narrow_light
when topic=home self.quarter=sump
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Light makes a very short visit to our lower windows. | I like a patch of wall that stays white even in the Sump shade.
b : Enough to read by? | What keeps it white?
a : Enough to thread a blue needle if you lay things ready. | An hour of my elbow now and again.

scene stingy_spool
when topic=prices|times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Pinching a penny feels different when there's scarcely a penny there. | I keep my saving cord tied round an empty scrap some weeks.
b : What can you spare? | Why keep the cord?
a : Thread ends. A sound knot still joins two. | Makes it quicker to start again.

scene private_dye
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.gossip / react.self / assess
a : Something's being passed about. I reckon talk can stain. | I heard a name I care to keep out of the wash.
b : Even a true word? | Yours?
a : A true stain is still a stain. | Any name at all would deserve the same.

scene open_work
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd trust #self.friend# to see my blueprints before I had a nail bought. | I'd put a seat by for #self.friend# at the first counter of my own.
b : Blueprints for a stall? | Even on a busy day?
a : Paper and charcoal. All the blue's in my head. | Especially then. I'd want one familiar face in view.

scene late_cart
when topic=times|work world.wagons=late
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A late wagon's hard to argue with. | News of a late cart makes me count my stores twice.
b : Who do you blame? | Does the count change?
a : I'd stop short of blaming the whole road. | No. But I don't spend the evening counting again.

scene heard_work
when topic=news world.news
does tell.news / react.self / assess
a : The part I heard clear out of #world.news_from# was this: #world.news#. | #world.news.capitalize#. That's what reached me from #world.news_from#.
b : Can you vouch for it? | Any more to go with it?
a : For those words as I heard them. | I'd spoil the colour by adding another coat.

scene not_welcome
when topic=newcomer
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : A city with two jobs empty always needs three backs. | I've got patience for a strange face until somebody calls our wages generous.
b : A hard welcome. | That would smart.
a : I'd give up half my bread sooner than half my day's work. | Come try a week's living on them.

scene loose_thread
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A loose thread has only two futures. | Look at #hem#. That's how I like my promises finished.
b : Cut or pulled? | Flat and firm?
a : There's a third if you're clever. Tuck it in a seam. | With enough turned under for a second chance.

scene song_steam
when topic=pastimes self.likes=singing
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like a tune with some steps in the middle. | I'd sooner sing into a yard than a big hall.
b : Steps for dancing? | What about the echo?
a : For the voice. A little climb works wonders on the last note. | In a yard I get my own voice back from several windows.

story unravelled_mark [topic=memories]
  : I sewed a secret saving mark inside my skirt.
  : Worked out I'd used better thread for the mark than for the pocket.
  b : Did the coins escape?
  : Only one. There's a second saving mark now, and it's a proper seam.

story sheet_sky [topic=weather|memories]
  : Once a gust lifted a sheet so high the whole sky looked square.
  : The lower corners floated off like a pair of waving paws.
  b : Where did it land?
  : Right over the sheet I was shaking. I packed two up with one great hug.

story knife_plums [topic=food|memories]
  : I cut a tart into portions with a length of clean thread.
  : The first piece came away straight as a rule.
  b : And the other pieces?
  : I never saw another. I had to show everybody how to cut the first one.

rule @air_corner
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Just enough water in the air to weigh down a loose hem.

rule @breathe
when concept=bark self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One note, one breath, then set to.

rule @warm_shoes
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Dry boot tops are worth getting up for.

rule @wall_glow
when concept=bark here.place=street
does aside
cooldown 8h
say There's a light on that wall worth borrowing.

dlg @1 resident.hub : Just come where the light reaches the bricks.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#. I'd know your outline even against the sun.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : Night plays tricks with the colours. My ears work as well as ever.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : Keep a clear yard between our elbows.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.working=yes self.job=laborer] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. It pays for the next length of cloth.
dlg @2 resident.job : I keep a part of each day's strength towards my first counter.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : This crossed my hearing from #world.news_from#: #world.news#.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : If you want a name, ask someone keen to leave finger marks.
dlg @1 resident.bye : I'll let you go while that light holds good.
graft resident.hub
choice May I see the blue square? -> open_square
node open_square
say Have a look. A dark scrap in a dim place tells you next to nothing. Lay that square beside it and there's the colour plain.
choice Why is a corner missing? -> lost_triangle
choice It looks brighter already. -> hub
node lost_triangle
say I wanted it for marking my best pocket. A square with three good corners still earns a living.
choice I'll remember the trick. -> hub
choice Farewell for now. -> bye
